# Branch cleanup proof (#369)

The shared proof adapter is `tools/branch_cleanup.py`, extracted from delivery
CLI logic under ADR 001's modularity principle; tools stay outside the runtime
dependency graph (`architecture/dependency-rules.md`).

A merged or closed PR identifies a candidate by name, not permission to discard
the current tip. Before recommending or performing cleanup:

1. Keep protected heads, open PR heads and heads with no closed PR.
2. Require current-tip ancestry in `origin/master` (or the equivalent GitHub
   compare against master). Missing refs, unavailable GitHub and comparison
   errors fail closed. Report unmerged/recreated tips prominently.
3. Squash-only and closed-unmerged tips are retained for explicit review.
4. Use `pr_delivery.py delete-closed --ref <branch>` for remote deletion: it
   re-reads the tip and deletes only while it is the verified SHA, with no
   force flag (AGENTS.md 5.1). Never delete a branch by hand.
5. Local cleanup must recheck ancestry at application time. Local branch
   deletion uses an expected old SHA; worktrees with unmerged HEADs stay put.
6. A push saying `* [new branch]` after delivery may have recreated a merged
   branch. Inspect PR state and start a new focused branch for new work.

This preservation rule overrides mandatory deletion/clean-clone wording in
older delivery guidance. A retained tip is a finding, never a successful cleanup.
